From e13a140f88409952b3eae16a627241bf22b38213 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:25:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Try-on screens: fix what the shopper review found on
 phones

The preview now arrives in one commit with its screen (no empty Suspense
frame), so on a 360x640 Android it lands on screen with focus on its
heading. The crop frame leaves "Use this photo" on short screens, the real
piece beside a preview is the stone in it, and the open-back Cushion Halo
shows its sizes and names the one it adds. A size picked during the wait
stays, and the stone-change button names it. Sold-out pieces lead with the
reason, error screens keep one ink button, Save uses press and hold in every
in-app browser, and the hub fetches its first photos first. The e2e gains a
360x640 slow-render walk that fails on the previous build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpEhS3XnffjKP5JTdNrd3V
