-- The result screen's code is fetched during the wait; its chunk is in
-  `optionalChunk.ts` so a failed fetch never triggers the stale-build reload
-  (which would lose the photo and a paid preview).
+- The result screen's code is fetched during the wait, and a finished preview
+  waits for it (at most 8 s) before the step changes, so the result is drawn
+  in one commit with its focus and scroll. Never put it back behind a
+  Suspense fallback: on a 360x640 Android, Chrome's scroll anchoring moved
+  the first preview 640 px above the screen and focus fell to <body>. Its
+  chunk is in `optionalChunk.ts` so a failed fetch never triggers the
+  stale-build reload (which would lose the photo and a paid preview); the
+  preview then shows in a plainer frame.
+- Photo prep draws the decoded <img> straight into the crop preview and the
+  1152x1536 frame; Chrome reuses its first decode for both. A reduced working
+  copy drawn once (the shopper review's SHOP-6 idea) measured SLOWER in an
+  interleaved A/B at 4x CPU in headless Chromium (median 2.15 s against
+  1.66 s from pick to consent), so it was not kept. The spec's 800 ms is
+  still unproven: time it on a real mid-range Android in the preview smoke.
+
+Where the build differs from the spec, on purpose:
+- `src/lib/tryon/share.ts` is the spec's `shareImage.ts` (share and save in
+  one file). "Save photo" opens the press-and-hold view in EVERY in-app
+  browser or Android WebView, not only iOS ones (uxStates SHARE FALLBACK
+  over userFlow 10: Android's Instagram and Facebook drop a blob: download).
+- PieceStrip resolves stones with its own `tryOnStone` / `pieceInStone`, not
+  `colourCards.ts`, which would pull the colour-card code into the TryOn chunk.
+- The open-back Cushion Halo shows the product page's US 5 to 9 chips (US 6
+  picked) and its fit line, and the button names the size it adds; the spec
+  had it go in as a silent US 6. The chosen size rides in the link (`&size=7`).
+- The device-limit message takes its number from the server's 429 (the
+  `TRYON_DEVICE_DAILY` secret), not from a constant in the page.
+- The e2e lives in this repo (`scripts/tryon/e2e.mjs` and its synthetic
+  fixtures), not on the harness branch as `tryonflow.mjs`; serve-local uses
+  ports 4541/4542. Whether it stays here is the owner's call.
 
